{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2UMXe7B5t72VsAQx2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XgzH9rN8ceAbVTcBFUCdRt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/xf5fb84-build/engine-repo/dist/handoff && sed -n 1,60p API-INDEX.md; grep -n \"shapeMesh\\|materialTile\\|E.View\\b\\|new E.View\\|Mode7.view\\|splitScreen\\|E.Arcade\\.\\|bootSplash\\|versionLabel\\|input.label\\|lastDevice\\|glyphs\\|rumble\\|pointer()\\|allowJoin\\|addPlayer\" API-INDEX.md | head -80","description":"Look up key engine API names in the index"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6763,"cache_read_input_tokens":129078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6763},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcbe5b02-218b-4276-a1cd-eeebf017e39a","uuid":"c842ff50-ae96-4e7a-ac21-c06a75f9feb7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:07.690Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2UMKF2qNagdGvzbRw3","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XgzH9rN8ceAbVTcBFUCdRt":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/xf5fb84-build/engine-repo/dist/handoff && sed -n 1,60p API-INDEX.md; grep -n \"shapeMesh\\|materialTile\\|E.View\\b\\|new E.View\\|Mode7.view\\|splitScreen\\|E.Arcade\\.\\|bootSplash\\|versionLabel\\|input.label\\|lastDevice\\|glyphs\\|rumble\\|pointer()\\|allowJoin\\|addPlayer\" API-INDEX.md | head -80","description":"Look up key engine API names in the index"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XgzH9rN8ceAbVTcBFUCdRt","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n116:- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen\n581:- `E.bootSplash(title = '')`: the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.current by default) or { view, ix, iy }. Returns { cx, cy, x, y, z, face: 'top' | 'side' } (the world point it meets) or null off the map. Cells only, as height() has them (not props, actors, or walls cut away)\n851:- `level.crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3)` †: start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more; 0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record\n1096:- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face looking up), curved (as on a turned face), band: 2 (the light: 0 dark .. 4 bright) }) -> { w, h, rgba (Uint8ClampedArray, top row first, v up the tile) }; null for an unknown material\n1099:- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +y, its own scale applied: place it with the placement's facing, scale and flip). The same parts as r.shape draws; null for an unknown shape\n1100:- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n1101:- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn once per face, the crate's sides and bark's ends: uv runs 0 to 1 across each face), pos, nrm, uv (Float32Arrays: three numbers a corner, three corners a triangle; uv two a corner, world units across the surface)\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183153__xf5fb84/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcbe5b02-218b-4276-a1cd-eeebf017e39a","uuid":"d1c22f8d-5a1e-4da3-ae94-08f61a6de4c8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:07.712Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `