{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017MxKhNrqixd9LxZUc91uEX","type":"tool_result","content":"91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1223:- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1225:- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n1226:- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n1227:- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n1228:- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n1229:- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1230:- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n1231:- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1232:- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1235:- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n1236:- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1237:- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1239:- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1240:- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1242:- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n1243:- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n1244:- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1245:- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n1246:- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n1247:- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n1248:- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1249:- `arcade.o`: the options\n1250:- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n47: *    new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit, saves } }), or leave them out (menu: false, fullscreen: false,\n871:   *  gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } }) */\n2377:    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\n2379:    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\n2527:    this.input.names = (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.controls) || null;\n2528:    if (this.o.corner !== false && (this.o.menu !== false || this.o.fullscreen !== false)) this._corner = makeCorner(this);\n2530:    if (this.o.menu !== false) new Shell(this, { system: true });\n2573:    const showM = !open && (this.o.menu !== false ? (!!(sh && sh._menu()) || main) && (!play || near || touch) : !!I._touchEl);   // (menu: false: the touch START alone)\n2962: *      new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [{ key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', value: true }] } }) and reads game.settings.hints.\n3022:   * game.settings: the player's choices, one property each (game.settings.volume), with the game's own (o.menu.settings)\n3126:  btn('Menu', () => { if (game.o.menu !== false) game.menu(); else game.input._tapCode('Act:menu'); }).innerHTML = cornerIcon(CORNER_ICONS.menu);   // (menu: false: the touch START)\n3802: *    new E.Game({ menu: { saves: true } }) puts Save (while saves.canSave: a JRPG sets it at a save point) and Load in\n3805: *    menu: { saves: { slots: 3, version: 2, migrate(data, from) { ...; return data; } } } sets them.\n3908:Object.defineProperty(Game.prototype, 'saves', { configurable: true, get() { return this._saves || (this._saves = new Saves(this, this.o.menu && this.o.menu.saves)); } });\n3911:HOOKS.pause = (sh, acts) => {   // the pause menu's Save and Load, with menu: { saves }\n3912:  const g = sh._game; if (!(g.o.menu && g.o.menu.saves)) return;\n9132: *    defaults). new E.Game({ menu: { items: [['Restart', fn]], settings: [...], controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill:\n9203:    this._sys = !!o.system; this._std = o.standard !== false && game.o.menu !== false;\n9494:    const acts = (name === 'pause' ? [['Resume', () => this.hide()]] : []).concat(v(s.actions) || [], name === 'pause' && this._std && v(this._game.o.menu && this._game.o.menu.items) || []).filter(Boolean);\n9516:    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcbe5b02-218b-4276-a1cd-eeebf017e39a","uuid":"4c1238b1-8b7c-4d88-93d4-f070165606a8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:16:39.461Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1223:- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1225:- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n1226:- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n1227:- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n1228:- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n1229:- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n1230:- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n1231:- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n1232:- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1235:- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n1236:- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n1237:- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1239:- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n1240:- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1242:- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n1243:- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n1244:- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n1245:- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n1246:- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n1247:- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n1248:- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n1249:- `arcade.o`: the options\n1250:- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n47: *    new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit, saves } }), or leave them out (menu: false, fullscreen: false,\n871:   *  gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } }) */\n2377:    /** the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved\n2379:    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\n2527:  