{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghAcAhgBZkXVbQnKF5WL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013ZzJ5k2gEj8Vp1gGEkUv5F","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"node tools/build.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 && (timeout 2400 node tests/run.mjs --playthrough > /tmp/xf5_all.txt 2>&1; echo FIN >> /tmp/xf5_all.txt) > /dev/null 2>&1 &\ncat > /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183153__xf5fb84/work/TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183153/engine/PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine patches (my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2)\n\n`engine/my-3d2dge.js` is the handoff's full engine with the patches below. `node tools/patch-engine.mjs` applies them to a\nfresh copy (each patch checks a `/*TC:name*/` marker, so it is idempotent). Every patch is covered by a test.\n\n| Patch | Where | Why | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `weapons`, `tip`, `foregrip`, `drawhd`, `drawclassic`, `cutlass` | `Humanoid` constructor, `tip()`, the arm solver, both weapon draw blocks | A light-gun shooter's enemies carry rifles, SMGs, shotguns, launchers, sniper rifles, a minigun, a harpoon gun and a flare pistol, and the bosses swing a cutlass; the engine only had sword, gun and staff. Long guns are guns with a length (`o.gunKind`, `o.gunLen`), so every existing gun path (rest pose, `point`, `aim`, `tip()`) keeps working; the left hand goes to the fore-grip while aiming. | gameplay › enemies (muzzle points from `rig.tip()`), screenshots |\n| `glyphs`, `glyphs2` | the STANDARD settings table, `Input` | TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs by default with a Settings option for Xbox's A B X Y. | ui › input (`R2` by default, `RT` with Xbox) |\n| `wheel`, `wheellabel`, `wheelbind`, `wheeldev` | the canvas `wheel` listener, `CODE_LABELS`, `BINDABLE`, `press()` | The mouse wheel switches weapons: a notch presses `WheelUp` / `WheelDown` for one step (when the scene doesn't zoom), they read \"Wheel up\" / \"Wheel down\", can be rebound, and count as the mouse for prompts. | ui › input (`next` on the mouse is \"Wheel down\") |\n| `bus` | `ChipAudio` | `audio.bus('sfx' \\| 'music')` gives the engine's buses, so the gibberish voice synth and the panned SFX obey the volume settings. | core › audio (headless no-op path) |\n\nThe renderer (Rail3D), the Sim and everything else are the game's own modules (`src/`), not engine changes.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Rebuild, start the full test run, write PATCHES.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":867156,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1249},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcbe5b02-218b-4276-a1cd-eeebf017e39a","uuid":"82165e96-d113-4f7d-84ca-fddc6d416a99","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:19:55.184Z","request_id":"req_011CghAcA7hYPHbzg1DCfYVW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013ZzJ5k2gEj8Vp1gGEkUv5F":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183153__xf5fb84/work/TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183153 && node tools/build.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 && (timeout 2400 node tests/run.mjs --playthrough > /tmp/xf5_all.txt 2>&1; echo FIN >> /tmp/xf5_all.txt) > /dev/null 2>&1 &\ncat > /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183153__xf5fb84/work/TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183153/engine/PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine patches (my-3D2dge handoff v0.85.2)\n\n`engine/my-3d2dge.js` is the handoff's full engine with the patches below. `node tools/patch-engine.mjs` applies them to a\nfresh copy (each patch checks a `/*TC:name*/` marker, so it is idempotent). Every patch is covered by a test.\n\n| Patch | Where | Why | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `weapons`, `tip`, `foregrip`, `drawhd`, `drawclassic`, `cutlass` | `Humanoid` constructor, `tip()`, the arm solver, both weapon draw blocks | A light-gun shooter's enemies carry rifles, SMGs, shotguns, launchers, sniper rifles, a minigun, a harpoon gun and a flare pistol, and the bosses swing a cutlass; the engine only had sword, gun and staff. Long guns are guns with a length (`o.gunKind`, `o.gunLen`), so every existing gun path (rest pose, `point`, `aim`, `tip()`) keeps working; the left hand goes to the fore-grip while aiming. | gameplay › enemies (muzzle points from `rig.tip()`), screenshots |\n| `glyphs`, `glyphs2` | the STANDARD settings table, `Input` | TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs by default with a Settings option for Xbox's A B X Y. | ui › input (`R2` by default, `RT` with Xbox) |\n| `wheel`, `wheellabel`, `wheelbind`, `wheeldev` | the canvas `wheel` listener, `CODE_LABELS`, `BINDABLE`, `press()` | The mouse wheel switches weapons: a notch presses `WheelUp` / `WheelDown` for one step (when the scene doesn't zoom), they read \"Wheel up\" / \"Wheel down\", can be rebound, and count as the mouse for prompts. | ui › input (`next` on the mouse is \"Wheel down\") |\n| `bus` | `ChipAudio` | `audio.bus('sfx' \\| 'music')` gives the engine's buses, so the gibberish voice synth and the panned SFX obey the volume settings. | core › audio (headless no-op path) |\n\nThe renderer (Rail3D), the Sim and everything else are the game's own modules (`src/`), not engine changes.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Rebuild, start the full test run, write PATCHES.md"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_013ZzJ5k2gEj8Vp1gGEkUv5F":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183153__xf5fb84/work/TideCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183153"}}}
