s, exactly, and stops where it differs (game.stateHash = () => [...] sharpens that).\\n' +\n    ' * 11. TESTS. new E.Game({ headless: true }) (the default in Node) runs with no screen: game.advance(1) runs 120 fixed\\n' +\n    \" *    steps at once, game.input.tap('jump') and hold('right') script input, game.debug = { snapshot() { ... } } is\\n\" +\n    \" *    your game's handle for tests and tools; game.stop(), start() and dispose() stop, resume and end it.\\n\" +\n    ' * Errors in your game are shown on screen and in the console (game.errors).\\n' +\n    ' * THE HANDOFF PACKAGE holds this file and what it needs (dist/handoff/ in the repo, my-3d2dge.vercel.app/handoff/):\\n' +\n    ' *    API.md, the card (read it whole; the single-file editions embed it), API-INDEX.md (every public name, one line\\n' +\n    ' *    each: search it), AI_GUIDE.md (the recipes), tools/check.mjs, filmstrip.mjs and replay.mjs, and game/, a\\n' +\n    ' *    template game with a headless test.\\n' +\n    ' * MORE, outside this file (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge; search it and take only what a game needs, its files\\n' +\n    ' *    are large): 325 curated motion clips and 2,548 motion-capture takes as readable key poses that play on any\\n' +\n    \" *    Humanoid (src/mocap/: the catalogs list every clip's tags and description, tools/anim-set.mjs cuts the ones you\\n\" +\n    ' *    want into a small set, src/mocap/mocap.js plays them), and Emberdeep (src/emberdeep/), a whole game of worked\\n' +\n    ' *    examples: monsters, bosses, heroes with bodies that are not people, skills. AI_GUIDE.md, \"Where to find more\",\\n' +\n    ' *    says how to search them and take what you need. Still objects and materials as data (r.shape, E.MATERIALS):\\n' +\n    ' *    docs/ASSETS.md, its recipe checked with tools/asset-sheet.mjs.\\n' +\n    ' */\\n' +\n    '(function (root) {\\n' +\n    \"'use strict';\\n\" +\n    '\\n' +\n    '/** TAU: 2π, a full turn in radians; DEG: π/180, one degre